From: Guan Xuetao <gxt@pku.edu.cn>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:09:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] target/dadao: Implement RD integer semantics (12
 instruction families)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace ILLI stubs with real TCG code for M1 RD integer instructions:
- §3.1.1: 128-bit add/sub (add.uo/add.so/sub.uo/sub.so)
- §3.1.2: Fixed-width add/sub (byte/wyde/tetra, signed/unsigned)
- §3.1.3: Self-increment add.si (riii format, 18-bit signed imm)
- §3.1.4: 128-bit multiply (mul.uo/mul.so)
- §3.1.5: Fixed-width mul/div/rem (byte/wyde/tetra/octa)
- §3.2: Compare (immediate cmp.ui/cmp.si + register cmp.*/cmp.*)
- §3.3: Logic (and/or/xor/xnor, byte/wyde/tetra/octa)
- §3.4.1: Shift (shl/shr, byte/wyde/tetra/octa, orrr+orri)
- §3.4.2: Extend (ext.s/ext.u, byte/wyde/tetra/octa, orrr+orri)
- §3.5: Conditional assign (cs.n/cs.z/cs.p/cs.eq/cs.ne)
- §3.6: Immediate set (set.zw/set.ow/or.w/andn.w)
- §3.7: Block assign (rd2rd)

Key design decisions:
- ILLI check before any TCG write (precise exception)
- store_rd(0, val) silently ignores writes to rd0
- Source snapshot: all sources read before any destination write
- Division by zero / INT_MIN÷-1: TCG conditional branch to ILLI
- Fixed-width ops: only N bits participate, high bits preserved per spec
- Compare: three-branch pattern (default 1, EQ→0, LT→-1)
- swym remains NOP, all excluded_m1 instructions remain ILLI stubs
